Current original Zero workflow (0.12)

Use the native tools on Linux or their .exe versions on Windows:
  zero-integrate PROJECT_DIRECTORY NEW_KERNEL.zero
  zero-build PROJECT_DIRECTORY NEW_OUTPUT_DIRECTORY NEW_KERNEL.zero
  zero-check PROJECT_DIRECTORY NEW_TEST_DIRECTORY
All destination paths must be new. The integrator preserves authored sources;
the builder checks its compiler fixed point and builds the original targets;
the verifier checks language behavior and host file operations in process.
See tools/integrate.ztext, tools/build.ztext and checks/README.ztext.
Read these documents with zero-text read FILE.

The notes below preserve earlier implementation and test history. Any old
shell/Python runner names, generated artifacts, JSON reports or commands are
historical references: they were removed from the active project and are not
current runnable instructions or current-release validation. Native host
checks do not replace BIOS/UEFI, persistence or physical-hardware testing.

Historical implementation notes

ZERO WM FULL HD RENDERER CHECKS

Run from the project root:
  bash review-tests/wm-renderer-hd/run.sh

The own Zero compiler builds the actual production renderer with isolated
hosted setup/finish fixtures. Host Python performs orchestration and an
independent pixel oracle; it is never part of the OS. ImageMagick convert
only stores directly rendered PPM data as PNG for viewing.

The source lives in wm/worker.zero.part. The existing common fixtures under
review-tests/wm-renderer/ provide an800x600 setup; this runner creates exact
physical1920x1080,960x540,800x600,640x480 and640x400 versions with additional
stride padding, framebuffer guards and a text-grid sentinel. It replaces
only the infinite loop and cooperative yields to obtain one complete frame.
Full generated Zero sources and internal binaries go to a fresh private
build/wm-renderer-hd.* directory. Logs and PNG fixture outputs go to
verification/wm-renderer-hd-0.8.1.

A1920x1080 software framebuffer exceeds the normal4MiB hosted arena. The
original Zero helper grow-host-16m.zero validates our current ELF/prologue
and raises only the fixture arena immediate to16MiB. This helper derives
from the already documented own bootstrap transition helper. The runner
verifies that all other executable bytes are unchanged and rejects empty,
invalid ELF and already-modified prologue inputs. Fixture processes receive
a64MiB stack limit, or the available hard limit if smaller (minimum32MiB).
The production compiler, loaders, kernel arena and boot image are untouched
by this helper. It is not used by a normal OS build.

legacy-worker.zero.part is the frozen0.8.0 source, used only as an independent
exact-pixel compact-mode regression baseline. Current and legacy fixtures
both use the own current compiler and identical setup. Tests compare tile
and scrolling outputs at800x600,640x480,640x400.

FullHD tests compare every physical pixel against the960x540 logical fixture
and verify all native2x2 groups, RGB/BGR byte equivalence,128-byte guards,
16-pixel stride padding and the cell-grid end sentinel. No screenshot is
upscaled to produce the FullHD outputs. These are host-renderer fixtures,
not virtual-machine screenshots. Firmware, input and scheduling require
separate VM verification. No user data disk is opened by these tests.
